  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "One of the factors of \\(x^4+2x^2+9\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x^2+3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x+1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x^2-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x^2-2x-3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^4+2x^2+9 &=(x^2+3)^2\\\\ &\\quad{}-(2x)^2\\\\ &=(x^2-2x+3)\\\\ &\\quad\\cdot(x^2+2x+3). \\end{aligned} \\] Neither factor appears among choices A through D.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite the polynomial as \\((x^2+3)^2-(2x)^2\\)",
        "Factor the resulting difference of squares and compare both factors with the choices"
      ],
